  "id": "DrugBank_DB00387 - MONDO_21095",
  "verbalization": "Procyclidine is implicated in the pathogenesis of Parkinsonian Disorder through a series of indirect but interconnected pathways. The evidence suggests that Procyclidine is associated with Basal Ganglia Disease and Hereditary Late Onset Parkinson Disease, both of which are linked to Parkinsonian Disorder. This implies that Procyclidine may exert a modulatory effect on the basal ganglia, potentially influencing the progression of Parkinsonian conditions. Additionally, Procyclidine is linked to Early-onset Parkinsonism-intellectual Disability Syndrome, which also leads to Parkinsonian Disorder via a pathway involving Levodopa. These findings collectively suggest that Procyclidine may contribute to the development of Parkinsonian Disorder through mechanisms involving dopamine regulation and neurodegeneration. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential role of Procyclidine in the pathophysiology of Parkinsonian disorders, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
